## Commands

Run `make help` to see all available commands.

| Command | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| `make install` | Install dependencies |
| `make build` | Build the application |
| `make run` | Run the application |
| `make test` | Run tests |
| `make bench` | Run benchmarks |
| `make lint` | Run static analysis |
| `make fmt` | Format code |
| `make clean` | Clean build artifacts |

## Rules and Conventions

- Keep Go code idiomatic and simple; prefer stdlib patterns before new abstractions.
- Use table-driven tests for branching logic and keep tests near the code they verify.
- Wrap errors with context (`fmt.Errorf("...: %w", err)`) and handle once at the right layer.

